WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.170
A huge group I never joined.

2
00:00:02.850 --> 00:00:04.470
Our mark sheet posted in

3
00:00:04.470 --> 00:00:05.230
the parents’ group.

4
00:00:05.830 --> 00:00:08.730
And now the “head teacher” wants airtime?

5
00:00:09.390 --> 00:00:11.290
What is going on tonight?

6
00:00:12.630 --> 00:00:15.030
Today: the settings and habits that

7
00:00:15.030 --> 00:00:17.330
make school groups safer — for you,

8
00:00:17.870 --> 00:00:19.690
your pupils and your colleagues.

9
00:00:21.130 --> 00:00:23.550
If you’re an admin — a member who can

10
00:00:23.550 --> 00:00:25.750
change the group’s settings — start there.

11
00:00:26.360 --> 00:00:29.540
In a notice group, let only admins send

12
00:00:29.540 --> 00:00:31.480
messages and edit the group’s details.

13
00:00:32.350 --> 00:00:35.330
Then turn on approval for new members, so

14
00:00:35.330 --> 00:00:37.370
nobody joins by link without a check.

15
00:00:38.610 --> 00:00:40.030
Next, your own account.

16
00:00:40.720 --> 00:00:43.560
In privacy settings, choose who can add

17
00:00:43.560 --> 00:00:46.420
you to groups — my contacts only stops

18
00:00:46.420 --> 00:00:48.360
strangers adding you to scam groups.

19
00:00:49.060 --> 00:00:52.380
And turn on two-step verification: a

20
00:00:52.380 --> 00:00:55.100
six-digit PIN that the app asks for when

21
00:00:55.100 --> 00:00:56.540
your number is set up on a phone.

22
00:00:57.790 --> 00:00:59.870
Two-step verification means a

23
00:00:59.870 --> 00:01:01.670
stolen text code isn’t enough.

24
00:01:02.390 --> 00:01:04.750
Without your PIN, a scammer can’t

25
00:01:04.750 --> 00:01:06.270
move your account to their phone.

26
00:01:07.580 --> 00:01:09.060
Think of the school notice board.

27
00:01:09.710 --> 00:01:12.470
Only the office pins notices, and

28
00:01:12.470 --> 00:01:14.490
nobody pins a pupil’s report card

29
00:01:14.490 --> 00:01:16.550
there for every visitor to read.

30
00:01:17.220 --> 00:01:19.040
A school group works the same way.

31
00:01:20.260 --> 00:01:20.740
Quick check!

32
00:01:21.380 --> 00:01:24.060
A parent posts the whole class mark

33
00:01:24.060 --> 00:01:25.340
list in the parents’ group.

34
00:01:25.860 --> 00:01:26.380
Is that OK?

35
00:01:27.640 --> 00:01:27.880
No.

36
00:01:28.450 --> 00:01:30.190
Members can usually see each other’s

37
00:01:30.190 --> 00:01:32.630
numbers and forward anything in seconds.

38
00:01:33.400 --> 00:01:36.040
Pupils’ marks, photos and phone

39
00:01:36.040 --> 00:01:38.340
numbers stay out of big groups.

40
00:01:39.050 --> 00:01:41.330
If you’re the admin, delete the post

41
00:01:41.330 --> 00:01:43.230
and message the parent privately.

42
00:01:44.640 --> 00:01:46.400
Now, that “head teacher”.

43
00:01:47.010 --> 00:01:48.670
Anyone can put a name and

44
00:01:48.670 --> 00:01:49.970
photo on a new number.

45
00:01:50.620 --> 00:01:52.560
“I’m in a meeting — send airtime

46
00:01:52.560 --> 00:01:54.520
urgently” is a common trick.

47
00:01:55.100 --> 00:01:56.520
Call the head teacher on the

48
00:01:56.520 --> 00:01:57.580
number you already have.

49
00:01:58.870 --> 00:02:01.330
If it’s a scam, warn the group, then

50
00:02:01.330 --> 00:02:03.750
report and block the number: open the

51
00:02:03.750 --> 00:02:06.350
chat, tap the name or number, and

52
00:02:06.350 --> 00:02:07.970
choose report or block.

53
00:02:09.290 --> 00:02:09.830
Your turn.

54
00:02:10.440 --> 00:02:12.340
Someone tricks a colleague into

55
00:02:12.340 --> 00:02:14.320
sharing her six-digit text code.

56
00:02:14.950 --> 00:02:17.030
Which setting protects her account?

57
00:02:18.440 --> 00:02:20.080
Two-step verification — yes.

58
00:02:20.750 --> 00:02:23.190
Remember: admins control the group,

59
00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:26.490
a PIN protects your account, pupils’

60
00:02:26.490 --> 00:02:29.090
details stay out, and urgent

61
00:02:29.090 --> 00:02:30.630
requests get a phone call.

62
00:02:31.820 --> 00:02:34.320
Try it in class tomorrow: ask pupils to

63
00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:36.780
design the rules for a class group — who

64
00:02:36.780 --> 00:02:39.900
posts, what is never shared, and what to

65
00:02:39.900 --> 00:02:41.100
do with a strange message.
